{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"indoor-saintless-conure","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n`test_dc_corpus_has_eligible_units_that_actually_change` invokes Pandoc for 232 eligible prose units but its only contract is existential: at least one eligible unit exists and at least one changes. Current local runtime is 7.887s/232 subprocesses; an exact short-circuit reaches both witnesses in 0.035s/1 subprocess. Forced identity-renderer and no-eligible mutations fail under both forms. This is exact existential evaluation, not corpus sampling, and matches `any(...)` practice in pytest, Django, and CPython. No tracker rejection was found.\n\n## Plan\n- Freeze the existing two existential postconditions and inventory the full-corpus property tests that independently retain corpus-wide conversion coverage.\n- Strengthen the existing test oracle to prove iteration stops after both witnesses exist while still failing when no eligible or no changed unit exists.\n- Implement exact short-circuit evaluation without changing `_render_unit` or product behavior.\n- Run held-out RED→GREEN, defect-seeded mutation, focused corpus tests, repository gates, and paired timing. Back-out is a Gerrit revert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test still fails if the stratum has no eligible units.\n- [ ] The test still fails if every eligible unit renders identically.\n- [ ] The test stops rendering immediately once both existential witnesses have been observed.\n- [ ] Full-corpus idempotence, no-decay, richness, and hardening coverage remain unchanged in their existing tests.\n- [ ] A defect-seeded non-short-circuit mutation returns the held-out oracle to RED.\n- [ ] Paired timing quantifies saved subprocesses and runner time.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, Gerrit LLM-Review +1, and Gerrit Verified +1 pass before merge.\n- [ ] The final ticket comment records RED/GREEN/mutation evidence and measured savings.","id":"d792-5507-9df0-4a5f","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ci","performance","ubuntu","test","pandoc"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Short-circuit existential Pandoc corpus witness"},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786671674423629001,"uuid":"c1ab71c1-e7c9-4132-9a3a-4e2578869a0b"}